      "content": "# Month Calendar — Chain Toggle Mock\n\n## Context\n\nThe habit details page (`HabitDetailScreen`) has two calendars: a GitHub-style year heatmap and a traditional `MonthlyCalendarGrid` (6 rows × 7 cols, day cells with completion dots).\n\nToday the month calendar shows each completed day as a standalone filled cell — there is no visual link between consecutive completed days. The chain (\"don't break the chain\") visualization only lives inside the small 7-day `HabitChainVisualizer` on the main habits list.\n\nThe user wants the month calendar to **optionally render chain connectors** between consecutive completed days, with a toggle to switch between:\n\n- **Plain mode** (current behavior — standalone cells)\n- **Chain mode** (new — thin habit-colored line drawn between adjacent completed days)\n\nGoal of this plan: produce a static HTML mock showing both modes side-by-side so the user can react to the visual before any React Native code is written.\n\n## Recommended Approach\n\n**Single HTML mock**, saved to `.superdesign/design_iterations/month_chain_toggle_1.html`, showing:\n\n1. Two month-calendar panels rendered side-by-side (or stacked on narrow widths)\n2. Left panel = **Chain OFF** (current production look)\n3. Right panel = **Chain ON** (new look with connectors)\n4. A toggle pill above each calendar to make the difference obvious\n5. Same dataset in both so the visual delta is easy to read\n\n### Visual Spec for Chain Mode\n\n- **Connector style:** 3px horizontal bar in `habitColor`, drawn at vertical center of the day cell, spanning the gap between two adjacent completed cells in the same week row.\n- **Within-week chains only (v1):** No vertical connectors across week boundaries — same constraint as the 7-day `HabitChainVisualizer` would suggest. The end-of-week cell's right edge has no tail; start-of-next-week's left edge has no tail.\n- **Today:** keeps its 2px ring; connector still attaches.\n- **Missed day:** breaks the chain (hollow circle stays, no connector touches it).\n- **Opacity:** connector at ~85% opacity so the day number remains readable underneath/around it.\n\n### Toggle UI\n\n- Small segmented control in the calendar header next to the month/year label: `[ Plain | Chain ]`\n- Default state: **Plain** (preserves current behavior for users who haven't opted in)\n- Persisted via the existing settings/preferences pattern (out of scope for the mock — just show the control)\n\n## Mock Build Steps\n\nFollowing the project's superdesign workflow:\n\n1. **Layout (text):** ASCII wireframe in the mock file's header comment showing both panels and the toggle.\n2. **Theme:** Use the project's existing light theme tokens (white card bg, gray borders) — pick a representative `habitColor` like `#10B981` (emerald) for the demo. No new `generateTheme` call needed since we're matching production.\n3. **Animation:** Connector fade-in (200ms ease-out) when toggling to Chain mode; chain \"draws\" left-to-right via a scaleX transform on each segment with 30ms stagger.\n4. **HTML:** Single file, Tailwind via CDN, no JS framework — vanilla JS for the toggle interaction so the user can click between modes in-browser.\n\n## Files\n\n**New file (mock only — not production code):**\n\n- `.superdesign/design_iterations/month_chain_toggle_1.html` — standalone HTML demo\n\n**Production files referenced (NOT modified in this step — only inspected for visual fidelity):**\n\n- `src/components/BinaryHeatmap/MonthlyCalendarGrid/MonthlyCalendarGrid.tsx:14` — grid container, where toggle would mount in real impl\n- `src/components/BinaryHeatmap/MonthlyCalendarGrid/CalendarDay.tsx:35` — day cell, dot rendering logic the connectors would attach to\n- `src/screens/HabitDetailScreen/components/CalendarTabContent.tsx:35` — embeds the grid\n\n## Out of Scope (Future Step, Not This Plan)\n\n- Wiring the toggle to a real preference store\n- React Native implementation of the connector layer (would be a `Connectors` overlay positioned absolutely within each week row, computed from `weeks[]`)\n- Cross-week vertical connectors\n- Animation tuning in React Native Reanimated\n- Applying the same toggle to the GitHub-style year heatmap\n\n## Verification\n\n1. Open `.superdesign/design_iterations/month_chain_toggle_1.html` in a browser\n2. Both panels render side-by-side at desktop width; stack at mobile\n3. Click the toggle on the right panel — connectors animate in/out smoothly\n4. Visually confirm: chains only span same-week completions, missed days break the chain, today's ring still visible\n5. User reviews and either approves the direction or requests visual changes before any production code is written\n"
